# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env.local and put your real token in it:
#
#   Mac / Linux:   cp .env.example .env.local
#   Windows:       copy .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is gitignored, so it will not be committed to your repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your Cesium ion access token.
#
# Get one at https://ion.cesium.com/tokens
#
# IMPORTANT — create a NEW token. Do not use the "Default Token" on your
# account. The default token cannot be edited or deleted and grants read
# access to every asset on your account.
#
# Your new token should have:
#   - the assets:read scope ONLY
#   - access restricted to only the assets this project uses
#   - allowed URLs restricted to http://localhost:5173 and your
#     https://your-project.vercel.app domain
#
# Using src/layers/tilesets.ts to add Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles or
# Cesium OSM Buildings? Add "Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles" and/or
# "Cesium OSM Buildings" to this token's asset list too — assets:read alone
# does not grant access to a specific asset.
#
# Read this carefully: this token WILL be visible to anyone who visits your
# deployed site. That is normal and expected for Cesium ion. It is safe only
# because you scoped it above. See README.md, "About that token".
VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=your_token_here
